								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Measured against a plain {{gtClass:SubscriptionRegistry}}:\n\n- **Subscribing and unsubscribing weakly is faster**: a weak subscription takes 1.1 µs instead of 2.7 µs, and when many subscribers come and go the mixed registry is about 10 times faster (683 page view models created on one page and unsubscribed: 10 µs instead of 96 µs per view model). A plain weak subscription creates a global finalization entry, and a plain {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} scans all subscriptions.\n- **Strong subscriptions are a little slower**: subscribing and unsubscribing takes 960 ns instead of 720 ns, partly because the lock is reentrant.\n- **Delivering an announcement** takes about as long as with a plain registry for a few subscribers (1.9 µs for one strong subscriber in both), and about twice as long for 100 or more weak subscribers, because the weak part is walked in two levels, subscribers and then their subscriptions. It never allocates more than the plain registry (2.8 KB instead of 3.5 KB for one strong subscriber, 3.5 KB instead of 3.7 KB for 1,000 weak subscribers), because only the subscriptions that handle the announcement are collected.\n- **Memory:** an empty registry takes 184 bytes instead of 128. Most announcers never get a weak subscriber and pay nothing more; weak subscriptions take about as much memory as plain ones.\n"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:25:43.574347+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:27:39.678176+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "srqY10pyQj6pFIQX5RMeNg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The measurements and where the overhead comes from are on the page \"Mixed subscription registry: design\"."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:26:41.217409+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:26:41.217409+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "QTIKvp6IQvOSA4guPcNYkg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# What it costs"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:25:43.574353+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:26:44.226107+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "9WQ7zlkySAODhJbiJnzLKQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} and {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#removeSubscription:|label=#selector}} remove the subscriptions completely ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#unsubscribeRemovesStrongAndWeakSubscriptions}}).\n- {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription>>#makeStrong|label=#selector}} moves a weak subscription to the strong part; as in Pharo, the weak subscription becomes the strong one, so references to it stay valid ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#makeStrongMovesWeakSubscriptionToStrongPart}}).\n- {{gtMethod:AnnouncementSubscription>>#makeWeak|label=#selector}} answers a new weak subscription in the weak part; as in Pharo, the old strong subscription object is not changed, so use the answered one ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#makeWeakInMixedRegistryBuildsEphemeronSubscription}}).\n- {{gtMethod:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription>>#subscriber:|label=#selector}} files a weak subscription under its new subscriber ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#changingTheSubscriberRefilesTheSubscription}}).\n- {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#useSubscriptionRegistry:}} moves an announcer to another registry with its subscriptions. Moved to a plain registry, weak subscriptions become {{gtClass:WeakAnnouncementSubscription}}s, and those with a block action become strong subscriptions. Moved into a mixed registry, old-style weak subscriptions keep their behaviour, so install the registry before subscribing."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:26:44.223898+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:26:44.223898+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "3aiugBtQSYWhBRYOaTEQmA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Changing subscriptions"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:25:43.574354+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:26:47.494745+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "qL9J06nTQkOZ84xtSbdiYQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- A dead weak subscriber can still receive announcements until the finalization process has removed it, shortly after the garbage collection that notices its death (a scavenge for young objects, a full collection for old ones), as with Pharo's weak subscriptions.\n- Holding a weak subscription does not keep its subscriber alive, unless its action references the subscriber, for example a block that captures it.\n- {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry>>#subscriptions|label=#selector}} answers a copy, an {{gtClass:Array}}; delivery reaches strong subscribers before weak ones.\n- As in Pharo's registry, announcements are matched under the registry's lock, so matching code such as a {{gtMethod:Announcement class>>#where:|label=#selector}} condition should be short. If such code changes the registry while it is matched, the registry matches again on its subscriptions as they are then.\n- A shallow {{gtMethod:Object>>#copy|label=#selector}} of a registry gets its own sets and ephemerons but shares the subscription objects with the original.\n- Never send {{gtMethod:Object>>#deepCopy|label=#selector}} or {{gtMethod:Object>>#storeString|label=#selector}} to an announcer, a registry or a subscription: they contain cycles, and both recurse until memory runs out. This is the same with Pharo's registries."
						}
					]
				},
